The '''Saurin''' were a [[species]] of [[Sentience|sentient]] [[reptile]]s from the [[planet]] of [[Durkteel]], in the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] of [[the galaxy]]. They had imposing, jagged [[Tooth|teeth]], knobby skin, and ridges along the length of their heads.<ref name="DB" />

On the [[Standard day|day]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Luke Skywalker]] met [[Han Solo]] and [[Chewbacca]] in [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina|the cantina]] of [[Mos Eisley]], two Saurin patrons were in the bar.<ref name="ANH" /> A Saurin named [[Gauron Nas Tal]]<ref name=":0" /> was a resident of [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]]'s [[Boba Fett's Palace|palace]].<ref name="DB" /> He worked as a combat trainer for Jabba. Even though Gauron worked for Jabba, he planned to kill him.<ref name=":0">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref>

{{Species-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Two Saurins appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], during the bar scene. On set, they were simply known as "Crockers" or "Gila-Men," but one of them was to have been given the proper name of "Gilaass."<ref name="Crockers">{{SWArchive|url=episode-iv/bts/article/f20030502/index.html|text=Cantina Roll-Call: Shedding Light on Some Alien Aliases|int=Cantina Roll-Call: Shedding Light on Some Alien Aliases}}</ref>

